      "notes": "**Energy Transfer (ET) news, 2026-09-29 to 2026-10-29**\n\n**1. Guidance / results**\n- No guidance change found in the window. The last raise was on 2026-08-04, before the window. Full-year 2026 Adjusted EBITDA guidance went to $18.8–19.1B from $18.2–18.6B. — 2026-08-04 — https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/0001276187/000127618726000033/ex991eterq22026.htm\n- Q3 2026 results are due 2026-11-03 before the market opens, with a call at 9:00 ET. That is after the window. — announced 2026-10-01 — https://www.businesswire.com/news/home/20261001987770/en/Energy-Transfer-Announces-Third-Quarter-2026-Earnings-Release-and-Earnings-Call-Timing\n- Consensus for Q3 is EPS of about $0.40 on revenue of about $30.98B. — date unknown — https://www.marketbeat.com/earnings/reports/2026-11-3-energy-transfer-lp-stock/\n- The distribution was raised for the 20th straight quarter, to $0.3425 per unit ($1.37 annualized). — 2026-10-22 — https://ir.energytransfer.com/news-releases/news-release-details/energy-transfer-announces-twentieth-consecutive-increase\n- ET announced a $2.625B bolt-on acquisition of Vaquero Midstream. Consideration is $1.95B cash plus about 33.3M new ET units. — 2026-10-06 — https://www.worldpipelines.com/business-news/08102026/energy-transfer-to-acquire-vaquero-midstream/\n- Another source dates the same announcement 2026-10-07. — 2026-10-07 — https://www.chemanalyst.com/NewsAndDeals/NewsDetails/energy-transfer-strikes-2-625b-vaquero-midstream-acquisition-44860\n- I found no pre-announcement or guidance update tied to the Vaquero deal.\n\n**2. Analyst actions**\n- Mizuho raised its price target to $26 from $25 (Buy). — 2026-10-13 — https://www.tipranks.com/stocks/et/forecast\n- Barclays maintained a $24 target (Buy). — 2026-10-15 — https://www.ad-hoc-news.de/boerse/news/corporate-news/energy-transfer-stock-barclays-keeps-usd-24-00-target-for-energy-transfer-stock/70364129\n- J.P. Morgan reiterated a $25 target (Buy). — 2026-10-09 — https://www.tipranks.com/stocks/et/forecast\n- Goldman Sachs maintained Hold with a $22 target. — 2026-10-07 — https://stockanalysis.com/stocks/et/forecast/\n- Scotiabank maintained Buy with a $24 target. — 2026-10-07 — https://stockanalysis.com/stocks/et/forecast/\n- Morgan Stanley reiterated Hold with a $25 target. — 2026-09-23, before the window — https://stockanalysis.com/stocks/et/forecast/\n- Consensus is Strong Buy with an average target of $24.74 (range $22–28) per S&P Global data. — 2026-10-08 — https://stockanalysis.com/stocks/et/forecast/\n- TipRanks shows an average target of $24.46. — date unknown — https://www.tipranks.com/stocks/et/forecast\n- I found no upgrades, downgrades or initiations in the window.\n\n**3. Litigation / regulation**\n- FERC's 2026-10-15 meeting agenda included rehearing and clarification requests from ET and Kinder Morgan. They concern a 2025-11-20 order on remedial relief for a vacated order. ET asked that recouped assessments include interest. The agenda summary does not state the outcome. — 2026-12-22 is the filing date given in the source, so the event date is 2025-12-22 for the filing; the meeting was 2026-10-15 — https://www.whitecase.com/insight-alert/summary-ferc-meeting-agenda-october-2026\n- The Rover/Stoneman House $20M FERC penalty case was closed by a Texas federal judge in July 2026, before the window. — 2026-07 (day unknown) — https://www.eenews.net/articles/federal-judge-puts-fercs-energy-transfer-enforcement-case-on-ice/\n- Vaquero deal approvals, such as HSR clearance, were not found.\n- Desert Southwest: FERC had completed scoping meetings along the route as of the Q2 release. — 2026-08-04 — https://ir.energytransfer.com/news-releases/news-release-details/energy-transfer-reports-second-quarter-2026-results-and-updates\n- No new lawsuits, fines or investigations found in the window.\n\n**4. Customer concentration**\n- No new customer wins, losses or contract changes found in the window.\n- Vaquero's system has about 100,000 dedicated acres and long-term fee-based contracts, with an average remaining term of about 10 years. — 2026-10-06 — https://www.citybiz.co/article/914620/energy-transfer-to-acquire-vaquero-midstream-for-2-625-billion/\n- Earlier contracts (all before the window):\n  - Oracle: about 900 MMcf/d to three data centers. — https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1276187/000127618725000116/ex991eterq32025.htm\n  - Entergy Louisiana: a 20-year agreement for 250,000 MMBtu/d. — same URL\n- Management said in August that new gas power-customer deals would likely be smaller laterals rather than projects like Desert Southwest. — 2026-08-04 — https://www.morningstar.com/stocks/energy-transfer-earnings-another-guidance-raise-strong-throughput\n- I did not find a customer-concentration disclosure in the window.\n\n**5. Insider activity**\n- No Form 4 transactions found inside the window. The latest I found are before it:\n  - Director Kelcy Warren bought 1,000,000 units in open-market purchases at about $21.26–21.27, with no 10b5-1 plan. — 2026-08-18 (earliest transaction date; the second tranche was 2026-08-19) — https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/0001276187/000119312526359388/ownership.xml\n  - Director James Perry bought 12,359 units at $20.2276. — 2026-08-07 — https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/0001276187/000119312526342811/ownership.xml\n- OpenInsider's list shows no sales and no other Form 4 transactions after those dates, but I did not check it against EDGAR. — date unknown — http://openinsider.com/ET\n\n**6. Product / competitive**\n- The Vaquero deal adds a 300-mile West Texas pipeline network and Delaware Basin gathering and processing assets. — 2026-10-06 — https://www.worldpipelines.com/business-news/08102026/energy-transfer-to-acquire-vaquero-midstream/\n- The Caymus processing complex could be expanded toward 1.2 Bcf/d. — 2026-10-06 — https://www.citybiz.co/article/914620/energy-transfer-to-acquire-vaquero-midstream-for-2-625-billion/\n- ET, Sunoco, SunocoCorp and USA Compression moved their primary listings to the Texas Stock Exchange. — 2026-10-05 — https://www.energytransfer.com/\n- Hugh Brinson Phase I was expected to reach 1.5 Bcf/d by 2026-09-01. I found no confirmation that it did. — 2026-08-04 — https://ir.energytransfer.com/news-releases/news-release-details/energy-transfer-reports-second-quarter-2026-results-and-updates\n- Competitor news: EQT agreed to acquire Range Resources in an all-stock deal. It is a producer-side deal and not directly about ET. — 2026-10-26 — https://naturalgasintel.com/news/eqt-positions-for-next-era-with-deal-to-create-us-natural-gas-giant\n\n**Gaps:** Search was limited, so I did not check EDGAR directly for 8-Ks or Form 4s filed in October. I also did not check the Vaquero press release's 8-K for expected accretion or closing timing.",
